<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joachim Ernest, Prince of Anhalt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1536–1586</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joachim Ernest, Prince of Anhalt, reunited all the Anhalt lands under his rule in 1570 and issued a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/common-law">common law</a> code for them. He was a Lutheran prince who maintained a strong court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a>. After his death his sons divided Anhalt in 1603 into the principalities of Dessau, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernburg">Bernburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kothen">Köthen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zerbst">Zerbst</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plotzkau">Plötzkau</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joachim-ernest-prince-of-anhalt.jpg" alt="Joachim Ernest, Prince of Anhalt" width="320" height="449" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dguendel · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ballenstedt,_Schloss,_Bildnis_Joachim_Ernst_von_Anhalt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
